[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Persistent]
[00:11.95]Why did Elizabeth tell Nigel that
[00:16.31]she was going to the dentist?
[00:21.15]I crossed the street to avoid meeting him but he saw me and came running towards me.
[00:28.80]It was no use pretending that I had not seen him, so I waved to him.
[00:35.03]I never enjoy meeting Nigel Dykes.
[00:39.28]He never has anything to do.
[00:42.91]No matter how busy you are, he always insists on coming with you.
[00:49.64]I had to think of a way of preventing him from following me around all morning.
[00:57.06]'Hello, Nigel,' I said 'Fancy meeting you here!'
[01:02.59]'Hi, Elizabeth,' Nigel answered.
[01:06.32]'I was just wondering how to spend the morning--until I saw you.
[01:13.20]You're not busy doing anything, are you?'
[01:17.43]'No, not at all,' I answered. 'I'm going to...'
[01:23.03]'Would you mind my coming with you?'
[01:27.01]he asked, before I had finished speaking.
[01:31.70]'Not at all,' I lied, 'but I'm going to the dentist.'
[01:37.57]'Then I'll come with you,' he answered.
[01:41.24]'There's always plenty to read in the waiting room!'
